<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Shelter</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 8)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>shelter
enter shelter
</pre>
<p>Builds a shelter out in the wilds, from what the land offers: a wooden 
shack in a forest, a grass hut in a field or a swamp, an igloo on snow or 
ice. It can't be built anywhere else, or indoors. Building one takes a 
little while and a good deal of endurance, and you must be standing.
</p><p>Enter it, and you are out of the weather, and out of sight of the room: 
a snug place to rest. It holds a few people, so your friends can crawl in 
with you.
</p><p>The better your skill, the longer it stands: from a quarter of an hour 
for a clumsy builder to forty minutes or so for a master. Then it rots, 
or melts, and collapses, and anyone inside is left in the open.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Enter</a>
